  "live_records": {
    "q-60316": {
      "dom_id": "step-q60316",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Theresa pours out $\\frac{7}{8}$ of the contents of an $8$-cup jug of orange juice for her family's breakfast. How many cups of orange juice did Theresa pour from the jug?",
      "worked_solution": "To find out how many cups of orange juice Theresa poured from the jug, we need to multiply $8$ by $\\frac{7}{8}.$ \n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{8}\\times 8=\\frac{7\\times 8}{8}=\\frac{56}{8}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{56}{8}=56÷8=7\n$$\n\nSo, Theresa poured $7$ cups of orange juice from the jug.",
