    "q-60319": {
      "dom_id": "step-q60319",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Ted made pizzas for his soccer buddies. He put $\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{lb}$ of cheese on each pizza. If he made $8$ pizzas, how many pounds of cheese did he use in total?",
      "worked_solution": "To find out how much cheese Ted used, we need to multiply $\\frac{1}{4}$ by $8.$\n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n8\\times \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{8\\times 1}{4}=\\frac{8}{4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{4}=8÷4=2\n$$\n\nSo, Ted used $2\\,\\text{lb}$ of cheese to make the pizzas.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
