    "q-150234": {
      "dom_id": "step-q150234",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "An electrician takes a $4$-meter-long electrical cable from which he has to cut a piece that is $\\frac{5}{6}$ of its length. How long will that piece be?",
      "worked_solution": "To find out the length of the piece to be cut, we need to multiply $4$ by $\\frac{5}{6}.$  \n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{6}\\times 4=\\frac{5\\times 4}{6}=\\frac{20}{6}\n$$\n\nWe then reduce this fraction to its lowest terms:\n\n$$\n\\frac{20}{6}=\\frac{20÷2}{6÷2}=\\frac{10}{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we then convert $\\frac{10}{3}$ to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n10÷3=3\\,\\text{R}\\,1=3\\,\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the piece will be $3\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{m}$ long.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
